      "reasons": [
       "A's schedule is a day-tabbed list that opens on today, and the booking form only offers classes that actually run on the chosen date. That is a considered, usable flow; B's form lets you pick any class on any date.",
       "A names the teachers for each class and shows the per-class cost of each bono. The copy is specific ('Se suda, y se sale con la cabeza despejada'), with no filler verbs and no emoji.",
       "B leans on template patterns: a hero stat row ('21 clases a la semana'), a decorative CSS sun-and-arch in place of real imagery, a four-up card grid with colored tags, ✓ checkmarks and a 'El más elegido' badge on a pricing card.",
       "B's schedule grid is mostly '—' cells, which is visually noisy, and it needs a 720px horizontal scroll on mobile.",
       "A's weak points: picsum placeholder photos of a lake and a waterfall with no link to yoga or Valencia, although they are flagged in comments as provisional, plus a staggered fade-in on the hero."
      ]
     },
