      "reasons": [
       "B's booking form fills the class select from the schedule in the page, so visitors can only pick a real session for the chosen day. A uses a generic class dropdown plus a date field.",
       "B names the teachers on each class and schedule slot (Lucía, Marta, Andreu) and explains why the phone is needed, which makes the copy less interchangeable.",
       "B lays out prices as a list with a dark featured row, and classes as a definition list beside an image. That avoids A's familiar four-card grids for both classes and prices.",
       "B costs itself points with random picsum nature photos (a lake and a waterfall) whose alt text has nothing to do with yoga, and with links to legal pages that may not exist.",
       "B adds a staggered fade-in on the hero. It respects reduced-motion settings but is still decorative."
